! mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap -- printed page 102:
! "***** FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.109, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP  CARD ID
! BH000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 102", and the column
! sub-header prints "LINE  LOCATION  BINARY OUTPUT  NAME  STATEMENT
! LOCATION" (the right-hand "LOCATION" is printed LCCATICN, which is
! this drum's O/C dropout in the form's own heading).
!
! NINETEEN LINES, AND THE COUNT IS MEASURED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! rightmost column prints the card serial: line 1 is BH000001 and
! line 19 is BH000019, so line N is serial BH00000N with nothing
! missing at either end.  Rows were located mechanically by an ink
! profile of the serial column run over the FULL PAGE HEIGHT
! (y=0..3299 at 300 dpi, not the top third): it finds exactly
! nineteen 30-pixel text bands, y=360..1289, and one more at
! y=3204..3231, which is the "IBM." in the form's bottom frame.
! The same profile run on the LOCATION, BINARY OUTPUT, data-
! description and NAME+STATEMENT columns finds NO band eight
! pixels tall or more anywhere below y=1300 -- only the form's own
! dashed rules.  The page really does stop at line 19.
! THE CARD SERIES CHANGES HERE: printed p.100 is BD000001-BD000016
! and this page opens BH000001, so a block of card series (BE, BF,
! BG) falls on printed p.101, which is the UNIT AREA TABLE
! DEFINITIONS page.
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS AND NOT ONE CARD COMPILES A
! WORD. <<<  Thirteen of the nineteen lines (5-9, 11-15, 17-19) are
! SYN cards; the other six (1-4, 10, 16) are comment cards.  The
! BINARY OUTPUT column prints "+00000000" on every one of the
! thirteen and the data-description column prints "BU,nn ,10" --
! that is the column working correctly on a definitions page, not a
! crop in the wrong place (docs/transcription_workflow.md says so,
! and printed pp.24, 98 and 99 set the convention).  SO THIS DECK'S
! ENTIRE CHECK SURFACE IS THIRTEEN SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING ROWS.
! There is no !CHECK block below and there must not be one: a SYN
! deposits no storage word, and a !CHECK manufactured from the
! commented-out card on line 10 would be a fabrication.
!
! >>> THERE IS NO SLC ON THIS PAGE AND THIS DECK DOES NOT INVENT
! ONE. <<<  Every location printed here is a SYN VALUE -- a relative
! word.bit offset into a file-area-table entry, printed with the
! trailing "+" that is the SIGN -- not a storage address.  The
! location counter is never touched, so printed p.102 neither
! advances nor interrupts the chain: whatever counter printed p.101
! leaves, printed p.103 inherits.  FIRST AND LAST PRINTED LOCATIONS
! on the page are 000000.40+ (line 5) and 000006.00+ (line 19), and
! they are offsets, not addresses.  The smallest is 000000.00+
! (line 6) and the entry described runs from word 0 bit 0 through
! word 6 bit 17.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! It is the S-PREFIXED FILE AREA TABLE, and printed p.85 already
! carried the T-PREFIXED one ("SYN CARDS FOR FILE AREA TABLE").
! That makes p.85 an independent, already-transcribed witness for
! five of these thirteen fields, read off a different page months
! of transcription earlier:
!
!      p.85 line  7  T IODRN  SYN(BU,18), 0.0    <->  line  6 here
!      p.85 line  8  T TOELO  SYN(BU,18), 2.0    <->  line 11 here
!      p.85 line  9  T DENMD  SYN(BU,2), 2.27    <->  line 12 here
!      p.85 line 10  T REELD  SYN(BU,3), 2.29    <->  line 10 here
!      p.85 line 11  T FMODE  SYN(BU,2), 2.48    <->  line 13 here
!
! Same length, same offset, four of the five the same spelling after
! the prefix.  Line 10 is the strongest of them: it is the REEL
! DISPOSITION card, commented out here, and it still reads
! SYN(BU,3),2.29 -- bit for bit what p.85 prints for T REELD.  The
! three ARC fields are the interesting disagreement: p.85 has
! T ORARC/T MXARC/T CUARC as SYN(BU,12) at 5.06, 5.38 and 6.06,
! while this page has S OR ARC/S MX ARC/S CU ARC as SYN(BU,18) at
! 5.00, 5.32 and 6.00 -- eighteen bits, word-aligned and half-word-
! aligned.  That is a REAL DIFFERENCE BETWEEN TWO TABLES, not a
! misreading, and a THIRD PAGE takes this page's side:
!   * the widths are printed three times each on this page --
!     statement "18", data description "BU,22", and the 32-bit gap
!     between 5.00 and 5.32 -- and both pages are transcribed from
!     their own ink;
!   * PRINTED p.99 LINE 52 IS "S ARC AD SYN(BU,18), 0.32", an
!     already-transcribed S-SERIES witness that an ARC address in
!     the S tables is EIGHTEEN bits, against the T series' twelve;
!   * and the fields line up on their LOW-ORDER ends.  p.85's
!     12-bit ARCs at 5.06 and 5.38 end at bits 17 and 49; this
!     page's 18-bit ARCs at 5.00 and 5.32 end at bits 17 and 49
!     too.  Same right edge, field widened leftward by six bits.
!     That is what a deliberate revision looks like, not a
!     transcription slip in either direction.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COMMENT CARDS -- WHICH LINES, AND HOW THEY ARE TOLD APART
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO TELLS DECIDE IT, AND THE DASH IS NOT ONE OF THEM.  A card is
! a comment card here when (1) its LOCATION and its BINARY OUTPUT
! are BOTH empty and (2) its fields DO NOT LINE UP with the rows
! that assemble.  Six lines satisfy both: 1, 2, 3, 4, 10 and 16.
!
! >>> DO NOT USE THE "-" IN THE FIRST CHARACTER CELL AS THE TEST.
! <<<  Four of the six (1, 3, 4, 10) print a "-" at x=2345..2368 in
! the 300-dpi render -- the cell where every assembling line prints
! the "S" of its name -- and TWO OF THEM (2 and 16) PRINT NOTHING
! THERE AT ALL, though they are plainly comments.  Printed p.101
! line 2 behaves the same way.  That cell is just CARD COLUMN 2 of
! a raw card image, which holds a "-" on some comment cards and a
! blank on others, so its presence is weak evidence either way and
! its absence is no evidence at all.
!
! THE DECISIVE TELL IS THE RAGGED COLUMN, and it is measurable.  The
! character pitch on this page is exactly 30 pixels at 300 dpi and
! the cells are 2345, 2375, 2405, ... with the STATEMENT field
! beginning at 2615.  An assembling card puts its eight-character
! name in cells 2345-2555 and its statement at 2615 -- line 11's
! "S TOE LO" is S, blank, T, O, E, blank, L, O in exactly those
! eight cells.  Line 10 instead reads "-" at 2345, blank at 2375,
! then S, blank, R, E, E, L, D in 2405-2585 and SYN at 2615: THE
! WHOLE CARD IS SHIFTED RIGHT BY ONE CHARACTER, because what is
! printed is the raw card with a "-" punched into column 1 and the
! original SYN card text following it.  That is what commenting a
! card out looks like on this listing.
!
! LINES 2 AND 16 ARE THE COUNTEREXAMPLES TO THE DASH RULE.  Both
! print nothing at all in cells 2345-2585 and begin at 2615 (line 2
! "-***** FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****-", line 16 "-ENTRIES
! FOR DISK ONLY"), so both are cards whose image is blank through
! about column 10 and whose text then starts where a STATEMENT
! would start while the NAME field is empty -- which is itself the
! misalignment, since no assembling card on this page has an empty
! name.  Both have empty LOCATION and empty BINARY OUTPUT, so both
! compile nothing.  Lines 1 and 3 are the asterisk rules of the box
! and line 4 is a bare "-".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ONE GLYPH I COULD NOT SETTLE BY MEANING: LINE 9's NAME
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 9's name is six characters printed CLOSED UP (cells 2345,
! 2375, 2405, 2435, 2465, 2495 all occupied, no blank), unlike every
! other name on the page.  It reads S E W A I L and its comment is
! "-LOOP BIT FOR $WAIT".  SO THE COMMENT ORACLE DOES NOT SETTLE IT:
! the comment's word is WAIT and the name's last letter is not T.
!
! WHAT IS CERTAIN.  The sixth character is L: a left stem with a
! bottom bar and NO top bar and no mid-height ink, against the T of
! "$WAIT" in the same row's comment, which has a top bar and a
! centred stem.  Ink dropout opens and shortens glyphs; it cannot
! add a bottom bar to a T.  Characters 1, 3, 4, 5 (S, W, A, I) carry
! none of this drum's hazard pairs.
!
! WHAT IS NOT CERTAIN IS CHARACTER 2.  I read it as E rather than L,
! and THE CASE IS WEAK -- weak enough that it is written down here
! as weak rather than argued into looking strong.  From a greyscale
! pixel dump of the cell at 1200 dpi:
!   * the cell contains a full-height left stem and a full bottom
!     bar, which both E and L have;
!   * it ALSO contains a SOLID dark mark across the upper right of
!     the cell, level with the top of the neighbouring S, and a
!     fainter one at mid height directly below it -- the two places
!     where E's upper and middle bars run and where an L has
!     nothing.  Measured at 1200 dpi with the cell spanning about
!     x=265..340, the stem ends at x=287, the top mark covers
!     x=303..320 and the mid marks x=298..315, so both sit in the
!     MIDDLE of the span a bar would occupy, not at one end;
!   * tesseract, run on the name alone, reads SEWAIL independently.
! Ink dropout can open or break a bar but cannot print one that is
! not there, which is the whole of the argument for E.
!
! AND HERE IS WHY IT IS STILL WEAK.  Neither mark TOUCHES the stem
! -- there is a clear gap of about eleven pixels at 1200 dpi
! between the stem's right edge and the start of each -- and
! neither reaches the right end of the cell, so an E here would be
! more damaged than any other character on the page; and the SAME
! pixel dump finds a faint speck at x=327..331 ABOVE the middle
! bar's level, where neither an E nor an L has any ink, so this
! cell demonstrably collects marks that no letter explains.  A
! SIXTH CHARACTER THAT PRINTS A
! CLEAN L IS NOT A CONTROL FOR THIS, and I am not offering it as
! one: a drum printer has a separate hammer per column, ink varies
! per CHARACTER and not per row, and printed p.85 line 12 is the
! standing proof -- a clean closed O in the comment beside an open
! C in the name, one row, one drum.  Nothing in the corpus
! references this symbol, so listing_oracle can never catch this
! and its !SYM below will pass forever whichever letter is right,
! because it compares my statement against my own reading.  SEWAIL
! is a word in no sense.  IF A LATER PAGE REFERENCES THIS FIELD,
! PREFER THAT PAGE'S SPELLING OVER THIS ONE.  The alternative
! reading is SLWAIL -- never SLWAIT or SEWAIT, the final L is not
! in doubt.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE OTHER ROUND GLYPHS, AND WHY NONE OF THEM IS IN DOUBT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page drops ink on round glyphs constantly -- every LOCATION
! on it is an octal field printed as "0000nn.nn+" and several render
! to the eye as "CCCCCC.CC+" (line 6 is "0C0000.0C+", line 12's
! binary is "+CCCC0C00").  A C cannot occur in an octal field, so
! all of those are zeros with certainty.  In the NAME column the
! COMMENT COLUMN IS THE ORACLE and it settles every one:
!   line  6  "S IOD RN"  <- "-IOD REFERENCE NUMBER"  (and p.85's
!                           T IODRN)
!   line  7  "S IO IND"  <- "-IO INDICATORS"
!   line 11  "S TOE LO"  <- "-TABLE OF EXITS LOCATION", Table Of
!                           Exits LOcation; both O's (and p.85's
!                           T TOELO)
!   line 13  "S F MODE"  <- "-FILE MODE"  (and p.85's T FMODE)
!   line 14  "S CW"      <- "-CONTROL WORD", so C not O
!   line 15  "S CCW"     <- "-COPIED CONTROL WORD", both C's
!   line 17  "S OR ARC"  <- "- ORIGINAL ARC"; the name reads CR ARC
!                           in isolation and is OR ARC.  This is the
!                           exact pattern printed p.85 line 12 set
!                           with T CRARC/-ORIGINAL ARC = T ORARC.
!   line 19  "S CU ARC"  <- "-CURRENT ARC", so CU with a C
!   line  5  "S ACT AD"  <- "-ACTUATED ADDRESS", ACTuated ADdress
!   line  8  "S INT AD"  <- "-INTERRUPTED ADDRESS"
! C/D gave no trouble: the D of "S IOD RN", "S IO IND", "S INT AD"
! and "S F DEN" prints the straight vertical left stem and squared
! corners, plainly unlike the stemless round C of "S CW".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT CHECKS WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * NO ROW IS A BINARY CHECK, because there are no rows.
! * EACH SYMBOL IS CHECKED TWICE BY THE PAGE ITSELF, which is a real
!   check of the digits though not of the card: the STATEMENT prints
!   the bit offset in DECIMAL and the LOCATION prints it in OCTAL,
!   and all thirteen agree --
!     0.32/.40  0.0/.00  1.09/.11  1.32/.40  1.57/.71  2.0/.00
!     2.27/.33  2.48/.60  3.0/.00  4.0/.00  5.00/.00  5.32/.40
!     6.00/.00
!   The data-description column gives a THIRD rendering of each
!   LENGTH and all thirteen agree too: BU,19/BU,23, BU,18/BU,22,
!   BU,5/BU,05, BU,1/BU,01, BU,2/BU,02, BU,64/BU,100.
! * FIVE FIELDS AGREE WITH ANOTHER TRANSCRIBED PAGE.  Printed p.85's
!   lines 7, 8, 9, 10 and 11 give the same lengths and the same
!   offsets for the T-prefixed IODRN, TOELO, density, REELD and
!   FMODE fields.  That is five of thirteen, and line 10's agreement
!   is with a card this page has commented out.
! * THE THREE ARC FIELDS ARE CORROBORATED BY A THIRD PAGE, not
!   orphaned by their disagreement with p.85: printed p.99 line 52
!   gives the S-series ARC address as SYN(BU,18), and p.85's 12-bit
!   ARCs end on the same bits (17 and 49) as these 18-bit ones, so
!   the two tables agree on the right edge and differ by a
!   deliberate six-bit widening.  That is three more of thirteen.
! * NOTHING ELSE CROSS-CHECKS.  S ACT AD, S IO IND, S INT AD,
!   SEWAIL, S CW and S CCW rest on this page's ink alone, and
!   SEWAIL's second character is the weakest thing in this deck.
! * WHAT THE VERIFIER DOES NOT COVER.  tests/verify_mcp_page.py
!   compares OFFSETS only ("assembled bit 32, listing bit 32").
!   The thirteen LENGTHS never enter it.  They rest on the eye plus
!   the statement/data-description agreement recorded above, and a
!   PASS must not be read as covering them.
! * NO SUBSTITUTIONS AND NO OMISSIONS AMONG THE CARDS THAT COMPILE.
!   strap_asm refused no printed spelling on this page.  "S CW"
!   assembles cleanly as the name SCW although CW is also an
!   opcode.  Nothing here needed the $KF/$CM0000/(CC*)DD class of
!   workaround.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY one of the nineteen line numbers carries an asterisk right
! after it ("5*", "19*"), as on printed p.99.  That is the line-
! number column's own mark, not the one that sits after a LOCATION,
! and no line here carries that second kind.  Line 12's comment is
! printed further right than the others, starting in the comment
! field at a later column; that is the card, not the crop.

! ---- FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS (box, lines 1-4) ----------------
SACTAD  SYN(BU,19), 0.32            ! line  5 -ACTUATED ADDRESS
SIODRN  SYN(BU,18), 0.0             ! line  6 -IOD REFERENCE NUMBER
SIOIND  SYN(BU,5), 1.09             ! line  7 -IO INDICATORS
SINTAD  SYN(BU,19), 1.32            ! line  8 -INTERRUPTED ADDRESS
SEWAIL  SYN(BU,1), 1.57             ! line  9 -LOOP BIT FOR $WAIT
! line 10 is "- S REELDSYN(BU,3),2.29  -REEL DISPOSITION", a card
! commented out in column 1.  It defines nothing and is not
! transcribed; printed p.85 line 10 carries the same field as
! T REELD SYN(BU,3),2.29.
STOELO  SYN(BU,18), 2.0             ! line 11 -TABLE OF EXITS LOCATION
SFDEN   SYN(BU,2), 2.27             ! line 12 -IOD DENSITY*01-HI,
                                     !          11-LO,00-NULL
SFMODE  SYN(BU,2), 2.48             ! line 13 -FILE MODE
SCW     SYN(BU,64), 3.0             ! line 14 -CONTROL WORD
SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0             ! line 15 -COPIED CONTROL WORD
! ---- ENTRIES FOR DISK ONLY (line 16, a comment card) -------------
SORARC  SYN(BU,18), 5.00            ! line 17 - ORIGINAL ARC
SMXARC  SYN(BU,18), 5.32            ! line 18 - MAXIMUM ARC
SCUARC  SYN(BU,18), 6.00            ! line 19 -CURRENT ARC

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- all thirteen SYN cards, as printed.
! LINE | LOCATION | BINARY OUTPUT | dds | NAME | STATEMENT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  5  000000.40+  +00000000  BU,23 ,10  S ACT AD SYN (BU,19), 0.32
!   line  6  000000.00+  +00000000  BU,22 ,10  S IOD RN SYN(BU,18), 0.0
!   line  7  000001.11+  +00000000  BU,05 ,10  S IO IND SYN (BU,5), 1.09
!   line  8  000001.40+  +00000000  BU,23 ,10  S INT AD SYN(BU,19), 1.32
!   line  9  000001.71+  +00000000  BU,01 ,10  SEWAIL   SYN(BU,1),1.57
!   line 11  000002.00+  +00000000  BU,22 ,10  S TOE LO SYN (BU,18),2.0
!   line 12  000002.33+  +00000000  BU,02 ,10  S F DEN  SYN(BU,2),2.27
!   line 13  000002.60+  +00000000  BU,02 ,10  S F MODE SYN(BU,2), 2.48
!   line 14  000003.00+  +00000000  BU,100,10  S CW     SYN(BU,64), 3.0
!   line 15  000004.00+  +00000000  BU,100,10  S CCW    SYN (BU,64), 4.0
!   line 17  000005.00+  +00000000  BU,22 ,10  S OR ARC SYN(BU,18),5.00
!   line 18  000005.40+  +00000000  BU,22 ,10  S MX ARC SYN(BU,18),5.32
!   line 19  000006.00+  +00000000  BU,22 ,10  S CU ARC SYN(BU,18),6.00
!
! THE SIX LINES THAT COMPILE NOTHING, for the record:
!   line  1  -  ****************************************************
!   line  2     -***** FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS  *****-
!   line  3  -  ****************************************************
!   line  4  -
!   line 10  -  S REELDSYN(BU,3),2.29        -REEL DISPOSITION
!   line 16     -ENTRIES FOR DISK ONLY
!
! THE TRAILING "+" after every location is the SIGN, printed as a
! suffix the way printed p.84's negative SYN prints "000001.00-".
! It is dropped in the !SYM lines below because listing_oracle's
! loc_bits parses a location as "word.bit" and has no sign field,
! and because every landed deck records the bare NNNNNN.NN.

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 102 ----------------
! Thirteen symbols and no rows.  A SYN deposits no storage word, so
! there is nothing for a !CHECK to look at and none is written.
!SYM   SACTAD   000000.40
!SYM   SIODRN   000000.00
!SYM   SIOIND   000001.11
!SYM   SINTAD   000001.40
!SYM   SEWAIL   000001.71
!SYM   STOELO   000002.00
!SYM   SFDEN    000002.33
!SYM   SFMODE   000002.60
!SYM   SCW      000003.00
!SYM   SCCW     000004.00
!SYM   SORARC   000005.00
!SYM   SMXARC   000005.40
!SYM   SCUARC   000006.00
